# See: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/
#
# These mirror the checkov skips documented in the Dockerfile itself. Both
# scanners raise the same two findings, and both are deliberate for a container
# action that runs once and exits.

# Specify at least 1 USER command with a non-root user.
#
# The action writes to $GITHUB_OUTPUT, which the runner creates and mounts into
# the container. Running as a non-root user risks losing write access to a file
# the runner owns, and there is no way to verify that short of a live workflow.
AVD-DS-0002

# Add HEALTHCHECK instruction.
#
# There is nothing to health-check: the entrypoint runs to completion and the
# container exits.
AVD-DS-0026
